other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:26:01-08:00","id":319154,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of what Max Roman was trying to do in Colorado.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T15:09:01-08:00","id":319396,"title":"","content":"Considering how difficult it is for Werewolves to regain Essence, here's hoping there's a lot they can do without having to spend it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T03:41:44-08:00","id":319790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=319396#post319396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how difficult it is for Werewolves to regain Essence, here's hoping there's a lot they can do without having to spend it...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something Lodges could exploit. A Gamir (Lodge of Garm) is the last to leave a battlefield? Give him his Glory in Essence points. A Shepherd puts himself or his pack at risk for the well-being of a Blooded? gets his Purity as Essence too. A Serthaha bloodily punishes an affront to his own? You get it (Honor dots).<br /> <br /> Either that, or if you don't want to tie stuff up to Renown categories, the above examples could replenish all of the werewolf's Essence reserve.<br /> <br /> Now you see why they're so sought out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-23-2014, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T10:41:00-08:00","id":320025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=319154#post319154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of what Max Roman was trying to do in Colorado.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is EXACTLY what Max Roman was trying to Do in Colorado. Our campaign in San Francisco revolved around that idea as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T03:04:11-08:00","id":323558,"title":"","content":"Please, ple-e-e-as, can we see now only one fight-oriented Facet (for Strenght Gift for examle)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T23:15:57-08:00","id":324240,"title":"","content":"Already too late on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T23:10:15-08:00","id":326676,"title":"","content":"So one thing I'd like elucidated upon is how the new harmony system will actually work in practice. I know that touchstones will be involved somehow and that you can sin in either direction, but I'm a little concerned about it mechanically. I think my friend put it best when he jovially suggested that murdering a bunch of Pure with silver would be fine as long as he ate a baby afterward.<br /> <br /> From what I've read so far, that might not be entirely inaccurate. I have no doubts it will produce a cornucopia of amusement and horror, but what other system(s) are in place to curb that kind of behavior?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T23:14:58-08:00","id":326678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=326676#post326676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one thing I'd like elucidated upon is how the new harmony system will actually work in practice. I know that touchstones will be involved somehow and that you can sin in either direction, but I'm a little concerned about it mechanically. I think my friend put it best when he jovially suggested that murdering a bunch of Pure with silver would be fine as long as he ate a baby afterward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am more than a little amused at your friends comment and I intend to shamelessly use it myself at some point in the future.<br /> <br /> As for how the new harmony system will work complete with mechanics, it is something I am eagerly waiting for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T07:44:39-08:00","id":326957,"title":"","content":"Apparently Sam and Dean have died 117 times. Though Mystery Spot probably ups the number a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:15:37-08:00","id":327347,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious what the new rites are going to use as a dice pool now that it's not harmony. Also I'm curious as to the mechanics of being at the extreme ends of harmony. If an uratha neglected one of their halves. But I'm a crunchy mechanics kinda guy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3905-llewyd42","name":"Llewyd42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:23:22-08:00","id":327351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Llewyd42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=327347#post327347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really curious what the new rites are going to use as a dice pool now that it's not harmony. Also I'm curious as to the mechanics of being at the extreme ends of harmony. If an uratha neglected one of their halves. But I'm a crunchy mechanics kinda guy</div> </div> </div> </div>Attribute+Skill+Renown?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T15:11:55-08:00","id":327418,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure the Rites spoiler blog post included some of the first draft rites along with indications as to their dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T21:36:56-08:00","id":327683,"title":"","content":"What kind of open design space is there for home brew content? By that, I mean, Vampire has devotions, where you can figure out unique powers from combining disciplines, demons have gadgets, it's one of the really cool things I've liked from 2nd edition content so far that there are very useful guidelines for making your own cool powers. Gifts don't seem to be very conducive to homebrew, because you have to come up with a whole gift wholecloth, rather than a single distinct power. Do you have any space in the template for distinct powers with useful examples that would help players make their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:56:26-08:00","id":327896,"title":"","content":"Rites and fetishes both fit into that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T03:11:06-08:00","id":328007,"title":"","content":"I'll personally let players develop milestone gifts when a werewolf has all the five gifts, so space for homebrew is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T05:54:03-08:00","id":328114,"title":"","content":"Another Q&amp;A is up!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> Ephemera [Werewolf: The Forsaken] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T14:58:38-08:00","id":328643,"title":"","content":"How 'bout them new First Tongue offerings, eh? I was curious which words ran through Ye Olde Grimm-Sumerianolator to make the new jaggling/gaffling terms.<br /> <br /> Also the tease about Helios having something 'more appropriate' than shapeshifters? Not the Quash.... Alien-phoenix-birdmen-angels? Maybe he just zaps people with lasers until they do what he wants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T15:18:53-08:00","id":328680,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong but I think I remember someone saying something about the Shadow not being particularly good for werewolves during the day, or maybe getting there was harder or something. Though not, as far as I recall, to the extent that all hunts must be nocturnal.<br /> <br /> Either way, Helios as an antagonist makes sense, considering the wolf/sun rivalry in myth. I'm pleased with the answers from all these q/a's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T21:24:36-08:00","id":328876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=328680#post328680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could be wrong but I think I remember someone saying something about the Shadow not being particularly good for werewolves during the day, or maybe getting there was harder or something. Though not, as far as I recall, to the extent that all hunts must be nocturnal.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e locus-crossing mechanics included a -2 penalty for daylight hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T22:06:21-08:00","id":328911,"title":"","content":"And in text of 1ed Shadow Realm there is mentioning that day &quot;is bad for visits&quot;. Let me look in to this, I read about it few months ago...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THE GAUNTLET<br /> What is the Gauntlet? Simply speaking, it\u2019s a barrier between the worlds of \ufb02esh and spirit. Some scienti\ufb01cally minded Ithaeur liken the Gauntlet to the static between radio frequencies on the dial, a necessary transition phase between <br /> one station and the next. Yet, this fails to explain why it\u2019s so much easier to cross it under the light of Mother Luna than the glare of Helios. <br /> Other Ithaeur view the Gauntlet as a physical reminder of the scars borne by both the Uratha and the world of \ufb02esh for the murder of Father Wolf and the loss of Pangaea. Dwellers in the physical worlds are barred from the spirit world unless they possess magic to keep their destructive in\ufb02uence from growing any stronger. Spirits \ufb01nd it hard to cross, both for their own protection and to prevent the creation of more hybrid creatures like the kinslaying race of werewolves. <br /> <br /> For the Uratha, crossing between the worlds should theoretically be nothing more than a matter of adjusting their focus from one world to the next. A moment\u2019s concentration, and they\u2019re across. On some occasions, crossings like that still occur, giving the lucky werewolf a taste of the days out of legend. Most of the time, though, the process of converting \ufb02esh to spirit and slipping through the wall between worlds is only possible near a locus. It takes some time, and often it isn\u2019t even possible until the werewolf can regain his focus. </div> </div> </div>Than it seams to imply that Helios do not think werewolves are good guardians of Flesh and Shadow, and that Gauntlet is, at least partially, of his doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T00:01:13-08:00","id":328961,"title":"","content":"Myth-wise, the Gauntlet arose with Father Wolf's death-howl. He was the barrier between realms in Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T05:46:21-08:00","id":329145,"title":"","content":"He <i>hunted</i> in the Border Marches pre-murder; instead of a Gauntlet, there was a realm blending the material and Shadow together, that anyone could journey through in select places. His death Howl turned these Border Marches into the Gauntlet. Werewolves like to pretend (&quot;this story is true&quot;) that anything inside was killed or trapped in place forever. This is mostly because werewolves can't move inside it - when you cross over, you experience a few seconds of hanging, paralyzed, in the Gauntlet's grey void before the world you're entering forms around you.<br /> <br /> But sometimes you can see things out of the corner of your eye, or catch an odd scent, while crossing over.<br /> The Gauntlet has life inside it, for a certain value of &quot;life,&quot; that most people treating it as a barrier and not a seperate realm of existence never see. It's part of the esoterica of the nWoD's cosmology, because while werewolves and mages suspect there's something there, and sometimes try to summon Gauntlet entities to varying degrees of success, none of our protagonist supernatural beings deal with them directly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:01:02-08:00","id":329150,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is the right place to ask, but why did Mother Luna choosed Silver when she cursed the Uratha? Why not Gold, Platinum or any other material? Where in the books can I find that information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4038-leopaiva","name":"LeoPaiva","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4038_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:12:26-08:00","id":329153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329145#post329145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">none of our protagonist supernatural beings deal with them directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the next presumptive question would be which antagonist supernatural beings deal with them?<br /> <br /> Usually the Beshilu are trying to gnaw the Gauntlet away, and the Azlu to wall it off it, though if its its own world now it seems like their goals might have changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:15:35-08:00","id":329155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeoPaiva</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329150#post329150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this is the right place to ask, but why did Mother Luna choosed Silver when she cursed the Uratha? Why not Gold, Platinum or any other material? Where in the books can I find that information?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watsonian explanation: Vanity, methinks. Since the light of the moon is often described as a silvery light, it makes some amount of sense.<br /> Doylist explanation: Because the werewolf myth has them weak to silver, and being cursed by a Celestine (pardon: Ilusah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) associated with silver seemed fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:29:57-08:00","id":329161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeoPaiva</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329150#post329150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this is the right place to ask, but why did Mother Luna choosed Silver when she cursed the Uratha? Why not Gold, Platinum or any other material? Where in the books can I find that information?</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver is the metal symbolically associated with the moon; she probably <i>couldn't</i> curse them to be vulnerable to gold, traditionally more associated with the sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329153#post329153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the next presumptive question would be which antagonist supernatural beings deal with them?<br /> <br /> Usually the Beshilu are trying to gnaw the Gauntlet away, and the Azlu to wall it off it, though if its its own world now it seems like their goals might have changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The antagonists chapter in 2e touches on this but I'd sorely love more wordcount in a future book to really delve into the relationship between Azlu, Beshilu and the Gauntlet.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T07:00:34-08:00","id":329177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329161#post329161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The antagonists chapter in 2e touches on this but I'd sorely love more wordcount in a future book to really delve into the relationship between Azlu, Beshilu and the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be great, all the werewolf antagonists have benefit from more depth. But with the Azlu and Beshilu, as just a matter of preference it bugged me how diametrically opposed their motives were, while still being so more grand and threatening to the World of Darkness, compared to the other shartha, whose impact in the world is minimal compared to what the big two could do.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's probably why they're the most two well known hosts, because they're the most dangerous and the most populous.<br /> <br /> I guess it would be cool to see a hunting ground that was dominated by one or the other, so we could see the actual impact of something like the Azlu making the Gauntlet in an area impenetrable, providing that's what they do now. I get the feeling it wouldn't be as disastrous as it was theorized to be in 1e (if someone knows of a book that details this in 1e, feel free to share).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2014, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T12:51:44-08:00","id":329481,"title":"","content":"I think I describe Beshilu at one point &quot;gnawing their tunnels within&quot; the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T13:30:23-08:00","id":329518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329177#post329177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that's probably why they're the most two well known hosts, because they're the most dangerous and the most populous.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they <i>do</i> the most. From what I remember of the other shartha descriptions, they generally don't actually do anything, as far as Uratha, et. al. have noticed. The crows just sort of watch and the snakes are super-secret, but the rats and the spiders are actively and constantly making changes that are pretty noticeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T13:54:57-08:00","id":329531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329518#post329518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they <i>do</i> the most. From what I remember of the other shartha descriptions, they generally don't actually do anything, as far as Uratha, et. al. have noticed. The crows just sort of watch and the snakes are super-secret, but the rats and the spiders are actively and constantly making changes that are pretty noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why the Famine-Bringer's bits are arguably the strongest contenders for numerical/priority claim to the &quot;Third Host&quot; moniker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T14:38:52-08:00","id":329557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329518#post329518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they <i>do</i> the most. From what I remember of the other shartha descriptions, they generally don't actually do anything, as far as Uratha, et. al. have noticed. The crows just sort of watch and the snakes are super-secret, but the rats and the spiders are actively and constantly making changes that are pretty noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. I think the fungal host just sits there and occasionally hassles werewolves who kill their hosts. I like them and all, but it's a pretty petty metaphysical duty for such an insidious and pervasive life-form. Though the worm hosts, who degraded morality in 1e, might go through a nice change if they end up degrading integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2014, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T21:32:17-08:00","id":329864,"title":"","content":"I would like to state of how much the way the current voting block is making me nervous. The vote is whether to change the terminology of the First Tongue. At first, I wanted it to stay the same because it's hard for me to pronounce the new versions. Then I notice that the new terms sounded a bit Arabian, like in Arabian Nights and RPGs set in a fictional version of the Middle East. Then that led to the crazy stuff that ISIS is doing. Given that werewolves love to hunt, I worry that the Uratha and the Pure would be seen as jihadist-like groups in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Looking at the ratings, I think my opinion won't matter anyway, but when they do get accepted as the Lexicon, I plead with Onyx Path to make them alternative terms than the official. When I think about Werewolf: The Forsaken, I don't want to be reminded of ISIS.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T21:45:46-08:00","id":329868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329864#post329864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the ratings, I think my opinion won't matter anyway, but when they do get accepted as the Lexicon, I plead with Onyx Path to make them alternative terms than the official. When I think about Werewolf: The Forsaken, I don't want to be reminded of ISIS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your runaway train of thought as concerns back-converted Ancient Sumerian terminology is kind of out of anybody else's hands and Dave's noted that if the new First Tongue terminology gets adopted the old bits will likely be picked up by Mage to replace the seldom-used courtly Rank names anyway.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the new terms, though, digging through the Sumerian dictionary's gotten me nowhere in trying to figure out the approximate translation for the shared root of the terms replacing the Gaffling varieties - I already had an inkling that Ensihim and Ensahim are drawing on En- meaning &quot;Lord,&quot; but does anyone care to guess or share what Hur- translates to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-04-2014, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T21:55:16-08:00","id":329875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329864#post329864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to state of how much the way the current voting block is making me nervous. The vote is whether to change the terminology of the First Tongue. At first, I wanted it to stay the same because it's hard for me to pronounce the new versions. Then I notice that the new terms sounded a bit Arabian, like in Arabian Nights and RPGs set in a fictional version of the Middle East. Then that led to the crazy stuff that ISIS is doing. Given that werewolves love to hunt, I worry that the Uratha and the Pure would be seen as jihadist-like groups in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-poqLVTeMpJ0/T5rmgR-TK6I/AAAAAAAAZZA/JAAaCDv96iM/s1600/422916_345092288869288_263751677003350_1020445_180701239_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T22:35:15-08:00","id":329895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329868#post329868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the new terms, though, digging through the Sumerian dictionary's gotten me nowhere in trying to figure out the approximate translation for the shared root of the terms replacing the Gaffling varieties - I already had an inkling that Ensihim and Ensahim are drawing on En- meaning &quot;Lord,&quot; but does anyone care to guess or share what Hur- translates to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing &quot;mountain&quot;: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kur\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kur</a> from <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninhursag\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninhursag</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T00:26:35-08:00","id":329927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329864#post329864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think about Werewolf: The Forsaken, I don't want to be reminded of ISIS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, it seems you've already made that mental link. I don't think anyone else has, and I'd suggest trying to not worry about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T02:18:40-08:00","id":329956,"title":"","content":"Sumerian and Arabic aren't directly related languages despite coming from the same area of the world. So beyond the incredibly problematic &quot;Arabic = terrorist&quot; mentality there, it's just insanely off base.<br /> <br /> Worrying about Forsaken using modified Sumerian roots for the First Tongue somehow making people think about ISIS is more convoluted than saying a game that uses Welsh terminology is going to make people think it is about the Troubles because, you know, it's all Celtic languages and people from the same group of islands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T03:28:23-08:00","id":329976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329864#post329864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At first, I wanted it to stay the same because it's hard for me to pronounce the new versions. Then I notice that the new terms sounded a bit Arabian, like in Arabian Nights and RPGs set in a fictional version of the Middle East. Then that led to the crazy stuff that ISIS is doing. </div> </div> </div> </div>This is more convoluted than some of the conspiracy theories I've heard.<br /> <br /> Back on topic: I think we still need an English translation for the ranks rather than &quot;First rank, second rank&quot; etc. What exactly does those terms mean, etymologically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T05:12:34-08:00","id":330029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329976#post329976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is more convoluted than some of the conspiracy theories I've heard.<br /> <br /> Back on topic: I think we still need an English translation for the ranks rather than &amp;quot;First rank, second rank&amp;quot; etc. What exactly does those terms mean, etymologically?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to do with your standing in the spirit food/threat chain, which we know, but I am not sure that even feral Sumerian spirit naturalists would have a naming system more complicated than above/below or something ordinal?<br /> <br /> A little google-fu on 'apex predators' quickly brought me to <a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trophic_species\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trophic_species</a> which doesn't help as far as a naming convention.<br /> <br /> For rule of cool there could certainly be epitaphs like 'First to Feed' for rank 4, 'Last to Scavenge' for 1's, but in general the practicality of a label like that depends on how static the ecosystem is. Until humans messed it up it was probably pretty unchanging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:02:35-08:00","id":330131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=316361#post316361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protectorates sound like the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mondragon_Corporation\" target=\"_blank\">Mondragon Corporation</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im Slowpoke, but I must to right - it is bad for me, cuz I hoped fo something like that:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Los_Zetas_Escudo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas\" target=\"_blank\"> Los Zetas - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:07:38-08:00","id":330154,"title":"","content":"I dont say, that they are not mad bastards, I just say, that they are cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:28:30-08:00","id":330179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329518#post329518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they <i>do</i> the most. From what I remember of the other shartha descriptions, they generally don't actually do anything, as far as Uratha, et. al. have noticed. The crows just sort of watch and the snakes are super-secret, but the rats and the spiders are actively and constantly making changes that are pretty noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the opportunity to write more material on the other Hosts were to come my way at some stage, what I'd probably want to do is a) give them a more active agenda that opens up more conflict with the Uratha and b) tie them into the Gauntlet as well. For me, the role the Hosts have in relation to that barrier-phase between worlds is what makes them particularly distinctive; take that away and they lose a lot of their interesting nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329864#post329864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to state of how much the way the current voting block is making me nervous. The vote is whether to change the terminology of the First Tongue. At first, I wanted it to stay the same because it's hard for me to pronounce the new versions. Then I notice that the new terms sounded a bit Arabian, like in Arabian Nights and RPGs set in a fictional version of the Middle East. Then that led to the crazy stuff that ISIS is doing. Given that werewolves love to hunt, I worry that the Uratha and the Pure would be seen as jihadist-like groups in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Looking at the ratings, I think my opinion won't matter anyway, but when they do get accepted as the Lexicon, I plead with Onyx Path to make them alternative terms than the official. When I think about Werewolf: The Forsaken, I don't want to be reminded of ISIS.</div> </div> </div> </div>I genuinely don't think that the Uratha and Pure will be seen as jihadists or associated with the Islamic State, and writers can't feasibly start policing our word-use to ensure that nothing Arabic-sounding comes through on the slim possibility some people might think 'terrorist'.<br /> <br /> Rather than dwelling on the IS when you make that mental connection, try and consider other elements of Arabic culture and history - perhaps their role in learning and science in the medieval period, or the region's role as a hub of trade between East and West over the centuries, or some of the fantastical pre-Islamic folklore and stories that emerge from Arabic cultures, or perhaps the spirit of self-determination and liberation that drove some of the Arab Spring revolutions. Such things are also not directly related to the Sumerian being used for the First Tongue, but they may at least offer you a more palatable mental association.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330131#post330131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im Slowpoke, but I must to right - it is bad for me, cuz I hoped fo something like that:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Los_Zetas_Escudo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas\" target=\"_blank\"> Los Zetas - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Zetas </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Protectorates are many and varied in their forms; Los Zetas and Mondragon are both viable examples to base a Protectorate on. What's worth noting is that Protectorates often form in response to something that can't be handled by individual packs; also, due to the nature of Uratha, they have a tendency towards shorter durations rather than longer ones. That's not to say Protectorates are flash-in-a-pan occurences (though some are) but, for example, the Bristol Protectorate has been around for ~250 years and is one of the oldest (perhaps even the oldest) in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T10:52:26-08:00","id":330341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330179#post330179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the opportunity to write more material on the other Hosts were to come my way at some stage, what I'd probably want to do is a) give them a more active agenda that opens up more conflict with the Uratha and b) tie them into the Gauntlet as well. For me, the role the Hosts have in relation to that barrier-phase between worlds is what makes them particularly distinctive; take that away and they lose a lot of their interesting nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:04:42-08:00","id":330347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329868#post329868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your runaway train of thought as concerns back-converted Ancient Sumerian terminology is kind of out of anybody else's hands and Dave's noted that if the new First Tongue terminology gets adopted the old bits will likely be picked up by Mage to replace the seldom-used courtly Rank names anyway.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the new terms, though, digging through the Sumerian dictionary's gotten me nowhere in trying to figure out the approximate translation for the shared root of the terms replacing the Gaffling varieties - I already had an inkling that Ensihim and Ensahim are drawing on En- meaning &quot;Lord,&quot; but does anyone care to guess or share what Hur- translates to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I sorry about that. I know nothing about Sumerian lingo, and I immediately thought Arabian because it's the earliest thing I know of that uses that type of pronounciation with their language. I'm not as educated as other people on this forum about this topic, but whenever I hear the language I think of every pop culture reference set in the Middle East because the same pronouncation is used there.<br /> <br /> I know it may be nothing, but my disorder wouldn't allow me to rightly be calm about this after be subjected to everything that these vocal minorities have done in the Middle East (on TV four the past fourteen years. I bet that there were some British players that were concerned in the 90s about playing with the Fianna, given that in the decade before, there was a radical Irish extremist group using car bombs to force the British out of Ireland. It was in the news during that time. When these terms are used, I don't hear &quot;Sumerian&quot;, I hear &quot;Arabian&quot;, and that flares up my &quot;irrational&quot; fears, as much as other players like me.<br /> <br /> And I don't like it when people brush off my concerns like that without consideration, like what ArcaneArts did. It's like laughing at a person with more serious problems than I do because it makes them feel better.<br /> <br /> So please, allow me the decency to use the old terms in Werewolf as the new terms offends me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:36:24-08:00","id":330383,"title":"","content":"With all due respect, What's stoping you? No one can tell you what words to use!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:39:45-08:00","id":330385,"title":"","content":"I'm not laughing.<br /> <br /> I just-I don't see why or how that would work. It felt like saying ISIS ruined reading the Arabian Nights because people would associate the two, which is admittedly an absurd comparison but at the same time....<br /> <br /> Look, I just don't see it, particularly in the demographic of people who actually play RPG's. I don't hear it either. I just can't make the same worried leap you can. The prospect seems absurd to me. I can not see this being a problem. I probably lack context on your perspective. No, that doesn't mean I want to hear it.<br /> <br /> You have a concern, that's fine-no one's forcing you to call them that at your table. Yes, having those be the terms in the book is a problem for you if it turns out that's how people react, but you can easily introduce the ranks with the old books and talk things out and explain things to them.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a real issue, but even if it is, it's one you can easily deal with. You just have to talk to people.<br /> <br /> But in short on the problem, it's too baffling to me to even understand the connection in the first place. Sorry if that's a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:44:05-08:00","id":330391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330347#post330347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I sorry about that. I know nothing about Sumerian lingo, and I immediately thought Arabian because it's the earliest thing I know of that uses that type of pronounciation with their language. I'm not as educated as other people on this forum about this topic, but whenever I hear the language I think of every pop culture reference set in the Middle East because the same pronouncation is used there.<br /> <br /> I know it may be nothing, but my disorder wouldn't allow me to rightly be calm about this after be subjected to everything that these vocal minorities have done in the Middle East (on TV four the past fourteen years. I bet that there were some British players that were concerned in the 90s about playing with the Fianna, given that in the decade before, there was a radical Irish extremist group using car bombs to force the British out of Ireland. It was in the news during that time. When these terms are used, I don't hear &quot;Sumerian&quot;, I hear &quot;Arabian&quot;, and that flares up my &quot;irrational&quot; fears, as much as other players like me.<br /> <br /> And I don't like it when people brush off my concerns like that without consideration, like what ArcaneArts did. It's like laughing at a person with more serious problems than I do because it makes them feel better.<br /> <br /> So please, allow me the decency to use the old terms in Werewolf as the new terms offends me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is forcing you to use the changed terms, but First Tongue was all over 1st edition of Forsaken as well, what with terms like Imnir, Farsil Luhal, and such.<br /> <br /> I am not trying to brush your argument aside, but Sumerian is not at all similar to Arabic, I recommend reading up a little on it, perhaps that will make it easier for you to separate the languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:37:31-08:00","id":330509,"title":"","content":"Btw nobody thoghts about one flaw of new Gauru form? I mean, too much God-stats: Stamina and you have to take only the common Renown for Tribe and Auspex and put the free dot in that - if you don't want to sack in any battle. It's look like you char-list were writen without you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T14:10:11-08:00","id":330529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330347#post330347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know nothing about Sumerian lingo, and I immediately thought Arabian because it's the earliest thing I know of that uses that type of pronounciation with their language. I'm not as educated as other people on this forum about this topic, but whenever I hear the language I think of every pop culture reference set in the Middle East because the same pronouncation is used there.</div> </div> </