forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330529#post330529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read this: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumer\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumer</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to this, I have finally read the word &quot;sexagesimal&quot; ...base-16 for the win <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T14:37:29-08:00","id":330545,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it base 60? You know like it's leftover in the seconds to minutes to hour ratio?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T14:49:01-08:00","id":330550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330537#post330537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody can stop you from using the old terms. If you want to do that? Go for it.<br /> <br /> The problem is your stating that you're doing so for incredibly racist reasons. And people are going to respond to that. You might not see it that way, but that's what you're doing. &quot;Arab = terrorist&quot; is pure and utter racism.<br /> <br /> Consider the offenses here. You're asking us to respect your right to be offended because you're clinging to racist stereotypes. Well... most of us are going to be pretty damned offended by said racist stereotypes. I think this needs some serious perceptive. Acknowledging that your preference is irrational doesn't defend your reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I want to thank those who are allowing me to use the old terms. I hope Onyx Path will allow the same discretion.<br /> <br /> Second: I don't think Arab = Terrorist. There are only a very vocal minority that are linked to terrorist groups. It's like thinking Old Testament = Westboro Baptist. I'm just saying that it concerned me because of all the hype on the major news channels. The majority of those living in the Middle East are just hard-working people. Don't just assume that a person is racist because of a single concern on their part.<br /> <br /> I will respect those that use the new terms, and I hope I'm not shut out by players when I use the Old Terms.<br /> <br /> I hope that Onyx Path speaks about this in respect for those who want the new terms and those who want the old standby when they write-up the spirits in 2E.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for the info on Sumerian language, but I must tell you that there will be players of the TL<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />R variety that will blow off the info like some conservatives do with certain aspects of science.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T15:26:14-08:00","id":330563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330545#post330545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't it base 60? You know like it's leftover in the seconds to minutes to hour ratio?</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw something about alternating base-10 and base-6 and was so intrigued by a new word that I stopped actually-reading to share. So maybe? &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> But you are right sixty. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T15:31:31-08:00","id":330564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330550#post330550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope Onyx Path will allow the same discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful, especially because it isn't &quot;discretion.&quot; They're not going to waste word count on the old terms for people that don't like the new ones. Just like they didn't was word count in VtR 2e on Predator's Taint when explaining its replacement Predator's Aura.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second: I don't think Arab = Terrorist. There are only a very vocal minority that are linked to terrorist groups. It's like thinking Old Testament = Westboro Baptist. I'm just saying that it concerned me because of all the hype on the major news channels. The majority of those living in the Middle East are just hard-working people. Don't just assume that a person is racist because of a single concern on their part. </div> </div> </div>Let's look at some of the things you've said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then I notice that the new terms sounded a bit Arabian, like in Arabian Nights and RPGs set in a fictional version of the Middle East. Then that led to the crazy stuff that ISIS is doing. Given that werewolves love to hunt, I worry that the Uratha and the Pure would be seen as jihadist-like groups in the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>You said your thoughts went &quot;Sumerian sounds Arabian&quot; to &quot;Arabian means the Middle East&quot; to &quot;Middle East makes me think about ISIS&quot; thus &quot;Werewolves might come off as jihadists.&quot;<br /> <br /> This was not phrased as, &quot;I am worried about how other people will perceive things,&quot; but as your personal thought process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I think about Werewolf: The Forsaken, I don't want to be reminded of ISIS. </div> </div> </div>Again, this is phrased as your personal problem. You don't want to associate WtF with ISIS because it uses Sumerian as the basis of First Tongue and people are voting for legacy cWOD terms to be replaced with First Tongue terms, and Sumerian makes you think of ISIS because of the previous line of thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not as educated as other people on this forum about this topic, but whenever I hear the language I think of every pop culture reference set in the Middle East because the same pronouncation is used there. </div> </div> </div>Again, a personal phrasing. Sumerian makes you think of media representations of Arabs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When these terms are used, I don't hear &quot;Sumerian&quot;, I hear &quot;Arabian&quot;, and that flares up my &quot;irrational&quot; fears, as much as other players like me. </div> </div> </div>Again, you hear &quot;Arabian&quot; (Arabic is the language by the way) and this is still about your fears. And then you bring up other people... who are these other people? Appeals to random people aren't very effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So please, allow me the decency to use the old terms in Werewolf as the new terms offends me. </div> </div> </div>The new terms <i>offend</i> you.<br /> <br /> So no. I don't buy you back tracking here. Your posts have made it clear that you associate Arab with terrorist. You acknowledge that this is a bad association, you acknowledge it is intellectually false, but you're also advocating that Onyx Path act on it anyway. Your asking to have the choice to avoid the new terms because of this association respected.<br /> <br /> You're asking the Onyx Path authors to change the text of the books so you don't have racist thoughts because you don't like having racist thoughts. I'm glad you don't like having racist thoughts. But that is <b>your</b> issue to deal with. The forum users don't have the ability - and can't - fix your irrational associations for you. The authors of gaming books can't fix it for you.<br /> <br /> And I didn't call you racist. I called &quot;Arab = terrorist&quot; racist. And &quot;Arab = terrorist&quot; is the lynchpin in what you're saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T15:55:43-08:00","id":330581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330564#post330564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doubtful, especially because it isn't &quot;discretion.&quot; They're not going to waste word count on the old terms for people that don't like the new ones. Just like they didn't was word count in VtR 2e on Predator's Taint when explaining its replacement Predator's Aura.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let's look at some of the things you've said:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You said your thoughts went &quot;Sumerian sounds Arabian&quot; to &quot;Arabian means the Middle East&quot; to &quot;Middle East makes me think about ISIS&quot; thus &quot;Werewolves might come off as jihadists.&quot;<br /> <br /> This was not phrased as, &quot;I am worried about how other people will perceive things,&quot; but as your personal thought process.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, this is phrased as your personal problem. You don't want to associate WtF with ISIS because it uses Sumerian as the basis of First Tongue and people are voting for legacy cWOD terms to be replaced with First Tongue terms, and Sumerian makes you think of ISIS because of the previous line of thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, a personal phrasing. Sumerian makes you think of media representations of Arabs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, you hear &quot;Arabian&quot; (Arabic is the language by the way) and this is still about your fears. And then you bring up other people... who are these other people? Appeals to random people aren't very effective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The new terms <i>offend</i> you.<br /> <br /> So no. I don't buy you back tracking here. Your posts have made it clear that you associate Arab with terrorist. You acknowledge that this is a bad association, you acknowledge it is intellectually false, but you're also advocating that Onyx Path act on it anyway. Your asking to have the choice to avoid the new terms because of this association respected.<br /> <br /> You're asking the Onyx Path authors to change the text of the books so you don't have racist thoughts because you don't like having racist thoughts. I'm glad you don't like having racist thoughts. But that is <b>your</b> issue to deal with. The forum users don't have the ability - and can't - fix your irrational associations for you. The authors of gaming books can't fix it for you.<br /> <br /> And I didn't call you racist. I called &quot;Arab = terrorist&quot; racist. And &quot;Arab = terrorist&quot; is the lynchpin in what you're saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in a sort of circle jerk, you implied that I'm racist because of said equation. Plus, the reason why I think Arabian when I see the words is that <b>NO ONE, BUT THE PEOPLE WHO ARE TELLING ME I'M WRONG, KNOWS IT'S SUMERIAN!</b> I don't know Sumerian, my Mom doesn't know Sumerian, my brother doesn't know Sumerian, and the guys that I game with doesn't know Sumerian. It's comments like yours that me feel like a high school graduate discussing literature with Harvard Valedictorians and I'm sick to death on this elitist snobbery. And to use the term &quot;racist&quot; for people who don't agree with people like you just makes me wonder why I spend my time discussing these topics. Plus, <b>I HAVE ASD</b>, okay? I won't get all the cues that you do, but it doesn't excuse the fact that you insulted me when I was trying to concede. This makes me hope that the Ghost Wolves are the third voice in 2E, because I don't want to be on EITHER side, if people are just going to troll each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:04:32-08:00","id":330626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330581#post330581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in a sort of circle jerk, you implied that I'm racist because of said equation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're making a racist argument. Whether it's because of ignorance, purposeful taking of such a position for reason besides person beliefs, poor phrasing, or being an outright racist? It doesn't really matter. What you're saying is racist. You can either say, &quot;yeah what I said was pretty racist,&quot; and fix it, or you can double down on it some more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, the reason why I think Arabian when I see the words is that <b>NO ONE, BUT THE PEOPLE WHO ARE TELLING ME I'M WRONG, KNOWS IT'S SUMERIAN!</b> </div> </div> </div>You clearly aren't familiar with Arabic either. Why do you see Arabic instead of, say: Farsi, Pashto, Kurdish, Aramaic, Hebrew, Turkish, or Berber?<br /> <br /> Also... you know else who's telling you it is Sumerian? The Open Dev blog posts. The Epherema article explains how the First Tongue was constructed from Sumerian in the second paragraph. The authors working on the WtF game line revealed this shortly after the game was released on the old forums, and is on the White Wolf Wiki, eluded to on TVTropes, and there are threads that discuss it on multiple related forums (both general ones like RPG.net and specific ones like this one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's comments like yours that me feel like a high school graduate discussing literature with Harvard Valedictorians and I'm sick to death on this elitist snobbery. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but no.<br /> <br /> Google, &quot;Werewolf the Forsaken First Tongue.&quot; My first hit? The White Wolf Wikia article on the First Tongue, that explains that the language the First Tongue is based on is Sumerian.<br /> <br /> You're not putting even the most simple effort into knowing what we're talking about. This isn't &quot;high school graduate vs Harvard Valedictorians.&quot; This is, &quot;person that didn't read yesterday's assigned reading vs. the students that did.&quot; That's not elitism. That's expecting people to actually read what's being discussed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to use the term &quot;racist&quot; for people who don't agree with people like you just makes me wonder why I spend my time discussing these topics. </div> </div> </div>I used the term racism because I honestly and 100% believe that some of the things you said were racist. Most posting history is full of me disagreeing with people. I don't sling around racist lightly.<br /> <br /> Don't accuse me of using the term racist to disguise my real intentions unless you're ready to back that up.<br /> <br /> I'm calling your statements racist because I think they're racist. That I disagree with you on whether or not the authors should change the old legacy spirit titles for First Tongue words is irrelevant to this. If that's all I really saw? I'd probably have said nothing. I said all I needed to when I voted on the poll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, <b>I HAVE ASD</b>, okay? I won't get all the cues that you do, but it doesn't excuse the fact that you insulted me when I was trying to concede. </div> </div> </div>Tell me you have ASD basically tells me nothing. ASD has a huge range of symptoms. I don't know what yours are. I don't know if you have a symptom that impacts this, or if you're trotting out your diagnosis as an attempt of a &quot;get out of jail free&quot; card. Sorry that other people have ruined this for you, but far too many people on the ASD (or at least claiming a spectrum diagnosis) on the Internet have tried to use their disorder as an excuse for bad behavior.<br /> <br /> You have ASD? Ok. But recognize that this does nothing to inform us about any accommodations that could help you in this communication environment.<br /> <br /> And, again, I am calling your arguments racist. Not you racist. That you're defending those statements is a problem yes, but if I just wanted to call you a racist and be done with it, I'd have done so in a single short post. As for your concession... I didn't interpret it as a concession. Claiming that the new terms offend you is not conceding that your statements on why are a personal problem you need to deal with instead of something to advocate other people change to make you happy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:23:46-08:00","id":330640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330509#post330509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw nobody thoghts about one flaw of new Gauru form? I mean, too much God-stats: Stamina and you have to take only the common Renown for Tribe and Auspex and put the free dot in that - if you don't want to sack in any battle. It's look like you char-list were writen without you.</div> </div> </div> </div>More power to an Uratha if they can stay longer in Gauru, sure. Doesn't that mean every Hunt, or even every fight, can be settled by going Gauru.<br /> <br /> In other news, I like using First Tongue in-character whenever I can get away with it. <i>Desh Kar. Iminir. Dah. Amdulim. Ensah.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 12-04-2014, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:30:05-08:00","id":330645,"title":"","content":"Here's a question that occurred to me: God-tier spirits, i.e. Incarna-level and up; are they still instant death encounters for wolves, or will there be published methods of combatting and maybe even defeating them now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:31:22-08:00","id":330646,"title":"","content":"I like First Tongue as well, but I admit that outside the name of the Tribes, I had some trouble memorizing it's terms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:56:06-08:00","id":330669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330646#post330646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like First Tongue as well, but I admit that outside the name of the Tribes, I had some trouble memorizing it's terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's always a problem when inventing languages. That said, I personally had a huge problem, and still have, separating jagglings and gafflings. <br /> But as long as there are English translations it is fine. To me at least. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:05:13-08:00","id":330677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330581#post330581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, <b>I HAVE ASD</b>, okay? I won't get all the cues that you do,</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, are you referring to Acute Stress Disorder or Autism Spectrum Disorder? Your responses are more in line with the former than the latter. There aren't any social cues you're missing here; it's entirely an intellectual discussion, and someone with a degree of autism should be thriving, not feeling trapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:42:43-08:00","id":330697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330645#post330645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question that occurred to me: God-tier spirits, i.e. Incarna-level and up; are they still instant death encounters for wolves, or will there be published methods of combatting and maybe even defeating them now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The GMC updated rules generally leaves such beings as being pretty damned hard to take on, but the idea has always been that defeating anything in that area means dealing with banes/bans to have any hope of doing so. 2e seems to be more clear I guess, but this doesn't look like it is a change more than a clarification. But I guess we'll see when either we get an answer/spoiler or the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330646#post330646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like First Tongue as well, but I admit that outside the name of the Tribes, I had some trouble memorizing it's terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Though some of it is just practice. There are lots of terms (gaffling and jaggling) I only know because of lots of time with them through the games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=330677#post330677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There aren't any social cues you're missing here; it's entirely an intellectual discussion, and someone with a degree of autism should be thriving, not feeling trapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Autism can interfere with successfully communicating about topics that are highly based in social interactions. Communicating about racism can be hard without some of the social cues of how to do so in a fashion that will avoid offending people by being to blunt/matter of fact about things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T06:52:58-08:00","id":331042,"title":"","content":"I think his whole- actually, rude to talk about someone in the third person, sorry- rather than talk about someone's inner workings let me try to be nonjudgmental here:<br /> <br /> Jackalope, I think the crux of this is that while forum-goers can understand your thought process, they don't share your concern. When I read the preferred table my first thought was that these terms sounded more 'Hollywood Farsi' than ones I was familiar with (Garmir and Imnir for example always sound more, I dunno, gutteral? Subjective. Anyway.). I had that thought and then voted yes anyway because First Tongue is awesome.<br /> <br /> You were responded to very strongly by other posters which got you on the defensive. Sorry that stressed you a bit. For the sake of the conversation as a whole, though, I think you should go back to your first post, pretend a bunch of other people at the table nodded awkwardly, and then tried to switch the topic: your perception isn't wrong (all you did was share a private impulse that made you uncomfortable) but as this is a helpful forum and when you offer up an inaccurate point of view, people try to help you correct it.<br /> <br /> So again, your premise? *headnod* Sorry I can't say I find it a concern, but in the end you play your own game: going to the developers to have them validate your experience is tilting at windmills. Hope you can continue to enjoy WW anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:48:47-08:00","id":331448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329864#post329864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to state of how much the way the current voting block is making me nervous. The vote is whether to change the terminology of the First Tongue.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. It's whether to change a mishmash of invented terms, archaic terms, and English words that have no explanation or reason for being in the game to a set of unified words that obey the rules of First Tongue that we've set out before (porto-Sumerian with Hebrew pluralisations, as we use for spirit plurals in some other places). It's not &quot;old First Tongue terms&quot; vs &quot;new First Tongue terms&quot; because the old terms aren't First Tongue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At first, I wanted it to stay the same because it's hard for me to pronounce the new versions. Then I notice that the new terms sounded a bit Arabian, like in Arabian Nights and RPGs set in a fictional version of the Middle East. Then that led to the crazy stuff that ISIS is doing. Given that werewolves love to hunt, I worry that the Uratha and the Pure would be seen as jihadist-like groups in the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you've posted this explanation, as it's such a self-evident load of complete bollocks with a side order of unexamined racism that I don't need to explain why I'm ignoring your complaint.<br /> <br /> Also, the language is &quot;Arabic&quot;, not &quot;Arabian&quot;. That correction has been made in this thread, that you haven't bothered to pick up on it shows how little esteem you have for people who speak Arabic, and those who live in North Afria and the Middle East, which people in the UK/America generally brand the &quot;Arab World&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T17:26:25-08:00","id":331616,"title":"","content":"I'm a huge fan of the new names! I could never keep the gaffling/jagglings in order, They sounded too alike and I would mix them up constantly! At least these new terms are different sounding and more immersive; so if I screw them up they'll still sound awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T17:29:32-08:00","id":332602,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a link to the new terminology lists? I need to add/catalogue/dissect them for the dictionary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Tra